Egan Arithmites is a half-minotaur wanderer out of [[Geography/Lorandris/index|Lorandris]], a man in his middle years, eight or nine feet tall, with copper skin crossed by old scars and a gray-shot beard. From the waist down he is furred black and stands on cloven hooves, so he goes unshod. He wears a long black overcoat and a black raiment and carries a long rifle and a sword that is also a gun. He follows [[Divinity/Outer Gods/The Compelled|the Compelled]], whose raiment is silver, and no one has said why his is not.

He captained a ship out of Lorandris until a song came into his head and into his crew's. They sold the ship and turned inward, and the [[Org/Singers of the Herald's Star|Singers of the Herald's Star]] gathered them onto the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]], where he handed out pamphlets and small stones marked with a trumpet and woke only now and then. When the strider walked the song loosened its hold; when it stopped it grew loud again. One of the crewmates he came in with has grown mandibles.

He carried a bone-carved necklace since before any of this, found at a convocation of pirate crews in Lorandrian waters. Black smoke gathered into hands inside it and pulled at his face. [[People/Argyle|Argyle]] read it as one of the [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/index|Ashen Pact]], and a spirit of [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]] did live in it: when the Party entered Egan's mind, it wore the necklace and set the memory's pirate crew on them. It was destroyed and the necklace broke with it.

Argyle burned the Herald's hold out of his soul, and [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] put the [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]] in its place, the first time the song has passed between listeners. Egan hears it now whether he wants to or not, and says only that he has accepted the Vocalist, though the power he wields and his black raiment remain the Herald's gift.

He has thrown in with the Party and sleeps in one of their outer rooms.
